; status: works — Peter Messer's cube-root-of-two construction [messer1986;
; hull2020 §2.3], axiom 7 (the cubic Beloch fold) in its folded state.
;
; A square is divided into three equal vertical strips by PQ (x=1/3) and RS
; (x=2/3). It is then folded so that corner .c lands on edge AB while the top of
; RS, the point .s=(2/3,1), lands on PQ — a single simultaneous fold, which is
; axiom 7. The landing point divides AB in the ratio AC/CB = ∛2, the side of a
; cube of twice the volume. Its position is the root of a cubic and is irrational
; (constructible by folding, not by ruler and compass); the shared-field kernel
; folds it exactly in milliseconds. Render --folded to see Messer's Figure 2.
;
; The thirds are built first with rational scaffolding. --pq is a pure VALUE
; binding (no `mark`): it only names the fold target below and scores
; nothing, so the crease pattern no longer carries it. The six landmark
; diagonals (--ac --db --d_mb --a_mt --c_mb --b_mt) still have to stay
; `mark`ed, because a meet (`*`) requires both operand lines to already be
; physical creases (`--l is not a physical crease, so it has no material
; mark to cross`) — dropping `mark` there breaks ._pq1/._pq2/._rs1/._rs2.
; --rs likewise stays a full mark: `.s = --rs * --cd` needs --rs's mark to
; reach the top edge, but shrinking it to `between ._rs1 ._rs2` hits
; "spans an internal crease" (both ends sit exactly on other landmarks'
; crossings — classify_mark_extent has no representation yet for a mid-face
; extent anchored at two different existing-crease vertices). The folded
; landing (AC/CB = ∛2) is unaffected either way.

paper square

step vertical_middle
mark --vm = map .a onto .b                ; vertical midline x=1/2 (axiom 2)

step thirds
._mb = --vm * --ab                   ; (1/2, 0)
._mt = --vm * --cd                   ; (1/2, 1)
mark --ac   = through .a .c               ; landmark diagonal
mark --db   = through .d .b               ; landmark diagonal
mark --d_mb = through .d ._mb             ; landmark
mark --a_mt = through .a ._mt             ; landmark
mark --c_mb = through .c ._mb             ; landmark
mark --b_mt = through .b ._mt             ; landmark
._pq1 = --d_mb * --ac                ; (1/3, 1/3)
._pq2 = --a_mt * --db                ; (1/3, 2/3)
--pq  = through ._pq1 ._pq2           ; left third line PQ : x = 1/3
._rs1 = --c_mb * --db                ; (2/3, 1/3)
._rs2 = --b_mt * --ac                ; (2/3, 2/3)
mark --rs = through ._rs1 ._rs2           ; right third line RS : x = 2/3
.s    = --rs * --cd                  ; S = (2/3, 1), top of RS

step beloch_fold
fold map .c onto --ab and .s onto --pq   ; fold C onto AB, S onto PQ → AC/CB = ∛2

; neither landing is assertable in v1: `incident` always resolves against
; PAPER space (fixed, pre-fold — see test_bel_assert.ml's check_incident),
; not the folded TABLE position, so it can't confirm .s landed on --pq; and
; the TABLE landings are irrational in y (.c's x is a cubic root; .s's y a
; related irrational), so no exact rational literal matches either. The
; axiom7 tag and the no-temp-points invariant are covered externally by
; test_e2e_cube_root / test_e2e_cube_root_temps_hidden (kept, repointed here)
; assert faces = 2
; assert steps = 4
